# bw_kernel_syn project standards

- Language: **C++20** primary; Python optional (3.10-compatible APIs only).
- Framing: representation-aware **backward program synthesis**, not a single TT kernel.
- Never claim device behavior without measurement on pinned tt-metal.
- Never claim scale-separation novelty alone.
- Keep host build working without Tenstorrent SDK.
- Prefer small research IR; no LLVM/MLIR/RL/LLM unless forced by experiment.
- Update results tables with host/device labels separately.
- Before large claims or merges, consult roles in `AGENTS.md`.
- Before writing code: walk the **Ladder** (YAGNI -> reuse -> stdlib -> min that works). See `.cursor/CODE_STANDARDS.md` / Code Standards agent.
- No unused symbols; no restating comments; no decorative banners; propose new structure before creating it.
